1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:05,633
In the middle of the Pacific Ocean, more
than two thousand miles from California,

2
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:09,033
there is a chain of islands
that used to be a country.

3
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:15,467
It had a king, a flag, an army and treaties
with the great powers of the world.

4
00:00:15,833 --> 00:00:20,633
The Kingdom of Hawaii had embassies
abroad, a written constitution,

5
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:24,133
and one of the highest
literacy rates in the world.

6
00:00:24,567 --> 00:00:30,200
Then, in 1893, a small group of American
businessmen, backed by United States

7
00:00:30,267 --> 00:00:33,100
Marines, removed its queen.

8
00:00:33,167 --> 00:00:37,900
Five years later, the islands
belonged to the United States.

9
00:00:38,333 --> 00:00:41,933
A hundred years after that, the
United States Congress did something

10
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,767
it almost never does.

11
00:00:43,833 --> 00:00:45,367
It apologized.

12
00:00:45,433 --> 00:00:47,867
So how did America take Hawaii?

13
00:00:47,933 --> 00:00:52,667
It started, like so many stories
on this channel, with geography.

14
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:55,433
Look where Hawaii sits.

15
00:00:55,500 --> 00:01:00,267
Halfway between America and Asia,
alone in the biggest ocean on Earth.

16
00:01:00,333 --> 00:01:04,633
In the age of sailing ships and
steamships, every long voyage across

17
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:09,100
the Pacific needed a place to
stop for water, food and coal.

18
00:01:09,167 --> 00:01:11,167
Hawaii was that place.

19
00:01:11,233 --> 00:01:15,100
Whaling ships from New England
turned Honolulu and Lahaina into some

20
00:01:15,167 --> 00:01:18,067
of the busiest ports in the Pacific.

21
00:01:18,467 --> 00:01:23,333
The British explorer James Cook
reached the islands in 1778.

22
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:29,367
Soon whalers, traders and missionaries
followed, many of them from New England.

23
00:01:29,767 --> 00:01:33,633
A year after he arrived, Cook was
killed in a fight with Hawaiians at

24
00:01:33,700 --> 00:01:36,967
Kealakekua Bay, on the Big Island.

25
00:01:37,367 --> 00:01:43,533
By 1810, a chief named Kamehameha had
united all the islands into one kingdom.

26
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:47,833
Its flag still flies today, with
the British Union Jack in the corner

27
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:51,900
and eight stripes, one
for each main island.

28
00:01:52,333 --> 00:01:57,367
In 1820, the first American
missionaries arrived from Boston.

29
00:01:57,433 --> 00:02:02,467
They built schools and churches, helped
put the Hawaiian language into writing,

30
00:02:02,533 --> 00:02:06,300
and their families would soon become
some of the most powerful people in the

31
00:02:06,367 --> 00:02:07,933
islands.

32
00:02:08,933 --> 00:02:10,400
Then came sugar.

33
00:02:10,467 --> 00:02:14,100
The sons of the missionaries
became planters and businessmen,

34
00:02:14,167 --> 00:02:16,600
and Hawaiian sugar made them rich.

35
00:02:16,667 --> 00:02:19,933
Their biggest market
was the United States.

36
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:24,567
To work the fields, the planters
brought in tens of thousands of laborers

37
00:02:24,633 --> 00:02:29,267
from China, Japan, Portugal
and later the Philippines.

38
00:02:29,333 --> 00:02:33,467
Meanwhile, diseases brought by
foreigners had devastated the Native

39
00:02:33,533 --> 00:02:35,900
Hawaiian population.

40
00:02:36,267 --> 00:02:39,567
Before Cook arrived, there were
probably around three hundred

41
00:02:39,633 --> 00:02:41,667
thousand Native Hawaiians.

42
00:02:41,733 --> 00:02:45,967
A century later, only about
forty thousand were left.

43
00:02:46,033 --> 00:02:49,767
In their own country, they
were becoming a minority.

44
00:02:50,167 --> 00:02:55,633
In 1875, the kingdom signed a deal
with Washington: Hawaiian sugar could

45
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:58,233
enter the United States tax-free.

46
00:02:58,300 --> 00:03:02,800
A few years later, as part of renewing
that deal, the United States got

47
00:03:02,867 --> 00:03:07,400
something it wanted badly: the
right to use a harbor near Honolulu.

48
00:03:07,467 --> 00:03:10,233
Its name was Pearl Harbor.

49
00:03:11,233 --> 00:03:13,567
The king was David Kalakaua.

50
00:03:13,633 --> 00:03:18,067
He traveled around the world, put electric
lights in his palace before the White

51
00:03:18,133 --> 00:03:22,167
House had them, and tried to
keep his country independent.

52
00:03:22,233 --> 00:03:28,000
In 1881, he became the first reigning
monarch in history to travel all the way

53
00:03:28,067 --> 00:03:29,900
around the world.

54
00:03:30,333 --> 00:03:35,667
In 1887, a group of mostly American
businessmen with an armed militia

55
00:03:35,733 --> 00:03:38,600
forced him to sign a new constitution.

56
00:03:38,667 --> 00:03:43,233
It stripped most of the king's power
and gave the vote to wealthy foreigners,

57
00:03:43,300 --> 00:03:47,133
while most Asians and many
poor Hawaiians lost theirs.

58
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:50,600
People called it the Bayonet Constitution.

59
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:56,667
In 1891, Kalakaua died, and
his sister became queen.

60
00:03:56,733 --> 00:03:59,167
Her name was Liliuokalani.

61
00:03:59,233 --> 00:04:03,800
She wanted to restore power to the
monarchy and the vote to her people.

62
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:06,000
She was also a songwriter.

63
00:04:06,067 --> 00:04:11,933
Her song Aloha Oe is still one of the
most famous Hawaiian songs ever written.

64
00:04:12,367 --> 00:04:14,367
The businessmen moved first.

65
00:04:14,433 --> 00:04:18,267
A group of thirteen men called the
Committee of Safety declared the queen's

66
00:04:18,333 --> 00:04:19,600
government over.

67
00:04:19,667 --> 00:04:23,933
And the American minister in Honolulu
ordered about one hundred and sixty

68
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:28,633
sailors and marines from the
warship USS Boston to come ashore.

69
00:04:28,700 --> 00:04:31,133
The marines did not fire a shot.

70
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:36,133
But they were posted near the palace,
and everyone understood the message.

71
00:04:36,533 --> 00:04:39,033
The queen had soldiers loyal to her.

72
00:04:39,100 --> 00:04:42,133
But she did not want a war
with the United States.

73
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:46,100
To avoid bloodshed, she gave up
her power, not to the businessmen,

74
00:04:46,167 --> 00:04:50,900
but to the United States, hoping
Washington would put her back.

75
00:04:51,333 --> 00:04:55,967
A judge named Sanford Dole became
the leader of the new government.

76
00:04:56,033 --> 00:05:00,333
His cousin would later found
the Dole pineapple company.

77
00:05:01,300 --> 00:05:03,400
At first, it almost worked.

78
00:05:03,467 --> 00:05:07,633
President Grover Cleveland sent
an investigator, James Blount,

79
00:05:07,700 --> 00:05:09,500
to find out what happened.

80
00:05:09,567 --> 00:05:15,400
His conclusion: the overthrow could not
have succeeded without the American marines.

81
00:05:15,767 --> 00:05:20,433
Cleveland called it an act of war against
a friendly nation, and he asked for the

82
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:22,367
queen to be restored.

83
00:05:22,433 --> 00:05:26,967
But the new government refused,
and Congress would not act.

84
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:32,367
In 1895, supporters of the queen
tried to take the country back.

85
00:05:32,433 --> 00:05:33,600
They failed.

86
00:05:33,667 --> 00:05:37,700
The queen was arrested and
forced to give up the throne.

87
00:05:38,133 --> 00:05:42,433
She spent about eight months as a prisoner
in a single room of the palace where

88
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:44,600
she had once ruled.

89
00:05:44,967 --> 00:05:49,833
When annexation came up again, Native
Hawaiians fought back with paper.

90
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:53,700
More than twenty-one thousand of
them signed petitions against it.

91
00:05:53,767 --> 00:05:57,400
A treaty of annexation
failed in the Senate.

92
00:05:57,833 --> 00:06:00,167
Then came the Spanish-American War.

93
00:06:00,233 --> 00:06:04,167
American warships were heading to the
Philippines, and Hawaii was the perfect

94
00:06:04,233 --> 00:06:05,600
stop on the way.

95
00:06:05,667 --> 00:06:10,233
In 1898, Congress annexed the
islands with a simple resolution.

96
00:06:10,300 --> 00:06:11,333
No treaty.

97
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:13,667
No vote by the people who lived there.

98
00:06:13,733 --> 00:06:19,267
On August 12th, 1898, the Hawaiian
flag was lowered at Iolani Palace

99
00:06:19,333 --> 00:06:21,433
and the American flag went up.

100
00:06:21,500 --> 00:06:26,033
Many Hawaiians stayed home
that day, refusing to watch.

101
00:06:27,033 --> 00:06:30,900
Hawaii became the heart of
American power in the Pacific.

102
00:06:30,967 --> 00:06:37,000
That is exactly why Japan attacked
Pearl Harbor on December 7th, 1941,

103
00:06:37,067 --> 00:06:40,733
pulling the United States
into World War Two.

104
00:06:41,167 --> 00:06:45,933
More than two thousand four hundred
Americans were killed that morning.

105
00:06:46,367 --> 00:06:50,767
In 1959, Hawaii became the fiftieth state.

106
00:06:51,233 --> 00:06:54,100
More than ninety percent
of voters said yes.

107
00:06:54,167 --> 00:06:58,167
But the ballot only offered
statehood or staying a territory.

108
00:06:58,233 --> 00:07:00,167
Independence was not on it.

109
00:07:00,233 --> 00:07:05,367
Today, the Pentagon runs its whole
Indo-Pacific Command from Hawaii,

110
00:07:05,433 --> 00:07:08,067
watching over half the planet.

111
00:07:08,467 --> 00:07:13,167
And in 1993, on the hundredth
anniversary of the overthrow,

112
00:07:13,233 --> 00:07:17,933
Congress passed a resolution, and
President Bill Clinton signed it.

113
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:22,967
It apologized to Native Hawaiians
for the overthrow of their kingdom.

114
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:26,100
Look at the map one more time.

115
00:07:26,167 --> 00:07:29,633
Hawaii, the Panama
Canal, Greenland, Canada.

116
00:07:29,700 --> 00:07:33,667
Islands and passages in the middle
of the routes that move the world.

117
00:07:33,733 --> 00:07:39,533
Again and again, America has wanted
the same thing: the stepping stones.

118
00:07:39,933 --> 00:07:42,733
Hawaii is the one place
where it got all of it.

119
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:44,767
A kingdom became a state.

120
00:07:44,833 --> 00:07:50,067
And the apology, a century later, shows
that even the country that took it knows

121
00:07:50,133 --> 00:07:51,833
how it happened.

122
00:07:52,233 --> 00:07:56,767
Today, around ten million
tourists visit Hawaii every year.

123
00:07:56,833 --> 00:08:00,867
And a Native Hawaiian sovereignty
movement still argues that the kingdom

124
00:08:00,933 --> 00:08:03,533
was never legally given up.

125
00:08:04,533 --> 00:08:07,667
If you want to see the other
places on America's list,

126
00:08:07,733 --> 00:08:12,267
watch our videos on Greenland,
the Panama Canal and Canada.

127
00:08:12,333 --> 00:08:16,767
And subscribe, so you don't
miss what's behind the next map.
